  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Systematic Observations Financing Facility SOFF Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">a) Sustained GBON compliance in all SIDS and LDCs. Based on a GBON data gap assessment in 2020, it is estimated that more than 2000 surface and upper-air weather observing stations in SIDS and LDCs need to become operational and start exchanging data.
b) Substantial improvement of forecasting and climate reanalysis products delivered by Global Producing Centres operated by WMO member states 
c) Strengthened country capacity in LDCs and SIDS to effectively use the improved weather and climate prediction data, to inform actions that create socio-economic benefits and enable beneficiary countries to avert and minimise the impacts of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
